  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive low carbon transport in Thailand: towards a viable policy pathway for congestion charging</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will provide technical support, a feasible policy pathway and implementation roadmap to 
accelerate equitable, sustainable and low-carbon transportation in Thailand via congestion charging. Spanning 25 months, the project follows a mixed-methods and co-creative approach, building on the 2022 pre-feasibility study conducted under the TRANSfer project implemented by to investigate implications of the congestion charging scenarios to vulnerable groups, and consider broad societal costs and benefits including health and safety impacts. The main output will be an endorsed implementation roadmap for Bangkok. Consultations and training will also be undertaken with selected secondary Thai cities to scope further expansion of the model.</narrative>
  </description>
